{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794103993,"nonce":"UF1YtZJl6fHrmOnohgerJegwNK8=","title":"Show: the arrows never leave the side tables","message":"## Design\n\n**Aspect changed:** `doc/design/views.md`, \"Side tables are a stop\" (and any sentence elsewhere it makes wrong, e.g. in `tui.md`).\n\n- `↑` from the first side row **rings**, as `↓` from the last already does: the side tables are a region of `Tab`/`S-Tab` alone, like the box. Today it goes to the header (`showPage.up`, `tui/show.go`).\n- Not `↑` to the header: where the tables are drawn under the fields (the narrow layout), that jumps over the whole fields table, and even side by side the header is not where the person came from.\n- Not layout-dependent arrows: the keys are the same both ways, width alone deciding the layout.\n- `Enter` on the `links` row still moves into the link tables (it is not an arrow); `S-Tab` is the way back.\n\nDesign approved by Luis on 2026-11-07, in a combined review of four stories (box column, side-table arrows, $EDITOR, hints on the bottom line).","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}